From 8700f741629616bdc16848e49ffe7fecde6807d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pypto-x-agent <pypto-x-agent@local>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 01:03:58 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 118/144] fix(cuda): calibrate the event timer with a
 kernel-free sleep span

R2-D-01: the calibration span previously contained two kernels, so the
measured rate was coupled to workload time (~1.7-2.3% low versus a pure
sleep span) and kernel_seconds_corrected was conservative.  The
calibration now records start, sleeps, records stop and synchronizes with
no kernel inside the span; the three gate thresholds (3/3/5) and the raw
kernel_seconds semantics are unchanged.

R2-D-02: nvidia-smi formats memory.used as e.g. "4509 MiB", so the old
float() parsing always returned None.  Parse the numeric prefix, keep the
raw string in diagnostics.device_memory_used_before_raw.
